objective:
Please deploy this repository as it is: contracts only, on Ethereum mainnet. There is no token and no owner.

It holds four contracts, to be created in this order: WorkProof, WorkOrders, CrowdPots, Doorbell. Their constructor arguments are in docs/LAUNCH.md: three existing mainnet addresses (IMD, IdentityMD's WorkRegistry, and the Payroll contract of our earlier launch, number 1531), three references to contracts of this same launch, and six fixed values for the Doorbell (one bytes32, four amounts and times, one bool written 0 or 1). No argument is $owner: no contract has an owner, an admin or a setter.

Nothing has to be called after deployment. The constructors make no external call and check no code size, so they run on an empty chain. There is no proxy, no initializer, no pausing and no minting; the runtime bytecode holds no DELEGATECALL, CALLCODE or SELFDESTRUCT. forge test checks each of these statements (test/launch/LaunchManifest.t.sol).

The project builds with solc 0.8.26, EVM version cancun, optimizer 200 runs, via_ir, bytecode_hash = "none" and cbor_metadata = false, as foundry.toml already says. We believe no source file needs to change for the launch. docs/THREATS.md, section 11, says what we checked in this code after the changes your pipeline made to our first launch, and why each rule here is as it is.

One rule we ask you to leave as it is: CrowdPots.claimRefund and claimRefunds can be called by anyone for any contributor, a contract included. A chip can be made in another address's name (chipInFor), so a contributor may be a contract with no way to make the call itself. docs/DEVIATIONS.md, D7, gives the reasoning.

The manifest we expect (also in docs/LAUNCH.md, where a test checks it against the code):
{
 "kind": "evm_contracts",
 "contracts": [
  {
   "contract": "WorkProof",
   "constructorArgs": [
    "0xb6d0a187b050fa5bb0b87033a203f37becf4a775"
   ]
  },
  {
   "contract": "WorkOrders",
   "constructorArgs": [
    "0xd34a99bc0f67ae1bbd63c660e6d0b0dd03e263b7",
    "$contract:WorkProof",
    "0x6e4362a5cec59eb3f611af6b2d81915cf5b45f1f"
   ]
  },
  {
   "contract": "CrowdPots",
   "constructorArgs": [
    "0xd34a99bc0f67ae1bbd63c660e6d0b0dd03e263b7",
    "$contract:WorkOrders"
   ]
  },
  {
   "contract": "Doorbell",
   "constructorArgs": [
    "0xd34a99bc0f67ae1bbd63c660e6d0b0dd03e263b7",
    "$contract:WorkOrders",
    "0x7679ff00d2b015b122f4c00147c1004ea6657aada5fff65e72986b90c6869185",
    "1000000000000000000",
    "1000000000000000000",
    "250000000000000000",
    "604800",
    "1"
   ]
  }
 ],
 "notes": "Contracts only. No token, no owner, nothing to call after deployment. WorkOrders' third argument is the address of Payroll from our earlier launch, number 1531."
}

